      </div>
      <p>
        Because the offset is negative (−9), locations in Hawaii-Aleutian Daylight Time experience clock hours 9 hours after Greenwich observatory coordinates do. When London or Greenwich marks 12:00 PM (noon) GMT, locations in HDT are in pre-dawn hours at 03:00 AM HDT.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Image 1: Time Difference Infographic -->
